{"context": "published", "host": "www.josephsmithpapers.org", "showHeader": true, "footerStyle": "mini", "statusCode": 200, "uri": "letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830", "page": "3", "is404": false, "gallery": [{"image": "/52/52_ppallen_196_thumb.jpg", "page": "1", "label": "196", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/1"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_197_thumb.jpg", "page": "2", "label": "197", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/2"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_198_thumb.jpg", "page": "3", "label": "198", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/3"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_199_thumb.jpg", "page": "4", "label": "199", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/4"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_200_thumb.jpg", "page": "5", "label": "200", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/5"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_201_thumb.jpg", "page": "6", "label": "201", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/6"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_202_thumb.jpg", "page": "7", "label": "202", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/7"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_203_thumb.jpg", "page": "8", "label": "203", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/8"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_204_thumb.jpg", "page": "9", "label": "204", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/9"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_205_thumb.jpg", "page": "10", "label": "205", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/10"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_206_thumb.jpg", "page": "11", "label": "206", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/11"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_207_thumb.jpg", "page": "12", "label": "207", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/12"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_208_thumb.jpg", "page": "13", "label": "208", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/13"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_209_thumb.jpg", "page": "14", "label": "209", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/14"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_210_thumb.jpg", "page": "15", "label": "210", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/15"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_211_thumb.jpg", "page": "16", "label": "211", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/16"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD1", "documentSeriesTitle": "Letter to the Church in Colesville, 2 December 1830", "editorialPageNumber": "198", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/26086/26086-0003.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> in that place, it being the seat of Satan.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5023974960808323196\"><a href=\"#5023974960808323196\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans4\"><span id=\"documenttrans4\">4</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">The phrase “Satan’s seat” is used in the book of Revelation. JS may have used the phrase to describe <a href=\"/place/colesville-township-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Colesville</a> because throughout the summer of 1830 members and believers were persecuted there. (Revelation 2:13; see also Historical Introduction to <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-july-1830-a-dc-24\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-july-1830-a-dc-24\" poptitle=\"Revelation, July 1830–A [D&amp;C\n24]\">Revelation, July 1830–A</a> [D&amp;C 24]; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-to-newel-knight-and-the-church-in-colesville-28-august-1830\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-to-newel-knight-and-the-church-in-colesville-28-august-1830\" poptitle=\"Letter to Newel\nKnight and the Church in Colesville, 28 August 1830\">Letter to Newel Knight and the Church in Colesville, 28 Aug. 1830</a>.)</p><hr></div></div></aside> But blessed be the name of God, it also hath become the abode of our savior, and may you all be faithful and wait for the time of our Lord, for his appearing is nigh at hand. But the time, and the season, Brethren, ye have no need that I write unto you, for ye yourselves perfectly know that the day of the Lord so cometh as a thief in the night: for when they shall say peace and safety, then sudden destruction cometh [p. 198]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> in that place, it being the seat <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>of Satan.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7608316604575734313\"><a href=\"#7608316604575734313\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans4\"><span id=\"documenttrans4\">4</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">The phrase “Satan’s seat” is used in the book of Revelation. JS may have used the phrase to describe <a href=\"/place/colesville-township-new-york\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Colesville</a> because throughout the summer of 1830 members and believers were persecuted there. (Revelation 2:13; see also Historical Introduction to <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-july-1830-a-dc-24\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-july-1830-a-dc-24\" poptitle=\"Revelation, July 1830–A [D&amp;C\n24]\">Revelation, July 1830–A</a> [D&amp;C 24]; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-to-newel-knight-and-the-church-in-colesville-28-august-1830\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-to-newel-knight-and-the-church-in-colesville-28-august-1830\" poptitle=\"Letter to Newel\nKnight and the Church in Colesville, 28 August 1830\">Letter to Newel Knight and the Church in Colesville, 28 Aug. 1830</a>.)</p><hr></div></div></aside> But blessed be the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>name of God, it also hath <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>become the abode of our savior, <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and may you all be faithful <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and wait for the time of our <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Lord, for his appearing is nigh<span class=\"deleted\">t</span> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>at hand. But the time, and <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the season, Brethren, ye have <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>no need that I write unto <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>you, for ye yourselves perfectly <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>know that the day of the Lord <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>so cometh as a thief in the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>night: for when they shall <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>say peace and safety, then <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>sudden destruction cometh [p. 198]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/52/52_ppallen_198_thumb.jpg", "mediumImageUrl": "/52/52_ppallen_198_med.jpg", "largeImageUrl